  "findings": [
    "The complete29B overlap compares self.top with other.bottom using UCOMISS/JB, then other.top with self.bottom using UCOMISS/JAE before the existing2D tail. Both comparisons must be ordered >=; equality touches and proceeds, unordered must return false. Current negated < disjunction admits NaN incorrectly.",
    "The original305B constructor checks finite X/Z dimensions and axis but does not reject Y dimension NaN. The proposed change must not add a global finite-height gate or change constructor semantics.",
    "The original5B get_closest_edge_id is only a tail jump to the complete726B closest edge pair body. The admitted existing private pair follows original first-pair/1000-distance/EPS/projection/tie policy; public wrapper should reuse its .0 instead of keeping independent infinity/squared loop.",
    "The full selected nearest595B source evidence is retained only as a caller dependency; this verdict does not change nearest algorithms."
  ],
  "approved_candidate_scope": "Only ordered Rectangle3d overlap predicate and Rectangle2d::get_closest_edge_id delegating existing closest_perimeter_edge_pair(point).0 plus truthful docs and meaningful literal-output tests. Do not alter private pair, 2D overlap, constructor, circle, shared point projection, perimeter methods or global geometry policy.",
  "required_tests": [
    "Actual public Rectangle3d constructor accepts NaN Y dimension; all four NaN vertical bounds and both argument orders reject; finite touching/overlap/separation and ordinary infinities preserve ordered behavior.",
    "Actual edge wrapper finite farpoint keeps edge0, translated/rotated witness, nearpoint edge2/center first tie/corner order, invalid-area failure uses existing as_points guard."
  ],
